===================================================
    
Case 1: CAST to NUMERIC of a NUMERIC(38,2) column has the size of a literal of the same value     

===================================================
cast(y as numeric)    disk_size( cast(y as numeric))    disk_size( cast(1.55 as numeric))    disk_size(y+0)    
1.55     8     8     8     

===================================================
    
Case 2: ROUND, TRUNC, FLOOR and CEIL of a NUMERIC(38,2) column have the size of their digits     

===================================================
round(y, 1)    disk_size( round(y, 1))    trunc(y, 1)    disk_size( trunc(y, 1))    
1.60     8     1.50     8     

===================================================
floor(y)    disk_size( floor(y))    ceil(y)    disk_size( ceil(y))    
1.00     8     2.00     8     

===================================================
    
Case 3: expressions whose common type is a floating NUMERIC convert the fixed side by its digits     

===================================================
nvl(y, z)    disk_size(nvl(y, z))    coalesce(y, z)    disk_size(coalesce(y, z))    
1.55     8     1.55     8     

===================================================
disk_size(case when z>0 then y else z end)    disk_size(decode(z, 1.5, y, z))    disk_size(greatest(y, z))    
8     8     8     

===================================================
disk_size( if(z>0, y, z))    disk_size(nullif(y, z))    
8     8     

===================================================
    
Case 4: UNION ALL and UNION with a floating NUMERIC column convert the fixed side by its digits     

===================================================
v    disk_size(v)    
1.5     4     
1.55     8     

===================================================
v    disk_size(v)    
1.5     4     
1.55     8     

===================================================
    
Case 5: a fixed value inserted or updated into a floating NUMERIC column is stored by its digits     

===================================================
0
===================================================
1
===================================================
1
===================================================
1
===================================================
id    v    disk_size(v)    
1     1.55     8     
2     1.55     8     

===================================================
    
Case 6: fixed columns of a negative scale and of scale 0 convert and round by their digits     

===================================================
cast(a as numeric)    disk_size( cast(a as numeric))    round(a, -6)    disk_size( round(a, -6))    disk_size( floor(a))    
1500000     4     2000000     4     4     

===================================================
cast(b as numeric)    disk_size( cast(b as numeric))    disk_size( floor(b))    disk_size( ceil(b))    
1500000     8     8     8     

===================================================
    
